  "finalAnswerPreview": "## Decision\\n\\nWhen a stored observation cursor is rejected, this workspace's integration should expect **`InvalidCursorError` from `@ordarium/core`, with stable `code === \\\"INVALID_CURSOR\\\"`** — a fail‑closed, terminal input/integrity failure, not a transient/busy condition, not `LEDGER_CORRUPT`, and **not** a silent restart from the beginning of the feed.\\n\\nIt is thrown by the state‑change‑feed read (`changes(filter, cursor)`, reached through `createStateStore(...).changes(...)`) when the cursor either cannot be decoded as a durable position or decodes to a position beyond the ledger's global high‑water mark.\\n\\n## Evidence (pinned artifact is decisive)\\n\\nThe workspace pins Ordarium **1.3.1** (`package.json`, `pnpm-workspace.yaml` overrides, `node_modules/@ordarium/core/package.json`), so the artifact, not prose, is the interface the integration compiles and runs against.\\n\\n- `node_modules/@ordarium/core/dist/src/errors.js` — `InvalidCursorError` → `\\\"INVALID_CURSOR\\\"`, message *\\\"The change cursor is not a valid durable position; refusing to guess a resume point\\\"*. The doc comment states it is **distinct from `LEDGER_CORRUPT`** (invalid caller input, not damaged ledger conte",
